	<h3>Transcriptomics Analysis &amp; Pipeline Engineering:</h3>
	<p>
	 End-to-end processing and analysis of short- and long-read RNA-sequencing data, transforming raw sequences (FASTQ), alignments (BAM/CRAM) or count matrices into biological discoveries. I implement custom, reproducible pipelines covering quality control, de novo transcriptome assembly, novel isoform annotation, alternative splicing, and differential expression. These workflows are optimized to deliver clear, publication- ready insights
	</p>
	<br>
	<h3>Population Genetics &amp; Large-Scale Association Studies:</h3>
	<p>
	Comprehensive quality control, processing, and statistical analysis for population-level variant datasets (VCF/BGEN/PLINK). Utilizing scalable cloud computing, I develop pipelines for Genome-Wide and Phenome-Wide Association Studies (GWAS/PheWAS), statistical fine-mapping, colocalization, and Mendelian Randomization. Backed by extensive experience handling multi-terabyte cohorts—including the UK Biobank and All of Us Research Program—I seamlessly integrate proprietary datasets with public repositories to deliver functional variant annotations and validated causal insights.
	</p>
	<br>
	<h3>Multi-Omics Integration &amp; Systems-Level Prioritization:</h3>
	<p>
	I build unified workflows that integrate diverse omics modalities to uncover systemic biological mechanisms and prioritize high-confidence leads. My expertise spans the joint analysis of genomics, transcriptomics, epigenomics, and RNA-protein dynamics datasets. By layering these molecular readouts with functional CRISPR/RNAi screens, I apply a unique systems-level perspective to translate fragmented multi-omic datasets into a single, cohesive map of gene regulation, variant impact, and macro-scale therapeutic or environmental pathways.
	</p>
	<br>
	<h3>Scientific Advisory, Data Visualization &amp; Strategic Review:</h3>
	<p>
	I provide strategic scientific oversight and high-impact data curation to accelerate research milestones, secure funding, and ensure project alignment. Leveraging over 20 years of cross- disciplinary experience, I translate complex multi-omic results into publication-ready visualizations and compelling data packages for grant submissions, manuscripts, and technical reports. Beyond data presentation, I conduct rigorous peer reviews of internal and public datasets, audit bioinformatics deliverables, and provide objective scientific advisory that synthesizes granular molecular data with macro-level project goals, ensuring data integrity at every stage of the research lifecycle.
	</p>
